---@alias vanta.manage_vanta.QuestionnaireResponseOriginType "AI"|"ANSWER_LIBRARY"|"MANUAL"|"ORIGINAL_QUESTIONNAIRE"|"RESOURCE"

---A questionnaire response without the fields that describe what the
---requesting user may do with it. Surfaces that authenticate a client rather
---than a user return this, since there is no user those fields could describe.
---@class vanta.manage_vanta.QuestionnaireResponseWithoutViewerPermissions
---@field id string The unique identifier for the questionnaire response
---@field sectionId? string|distilled.Null The questionnaire section this response belongs to, if any. Null for standalone questions or legacy responses without a section.
---@field sequenceLabel? string Sequence label for ordering responses within a questionnaire
---@field question string The actual question text
---@field editedBy? vanta.manage_vanta.CustomerTrustUser|distilled.Null The user who last edited the question/answer
---@field approvedBy? vanta.manage_vanta.CustomerTrustUser|distilled.Null The user who approved the current answer
---@field isPendingAnswerGeneration boolean Indicates whether the answer is currently being worked on by AI.
---@field originType? vanta.manage_vanta.QuestionnaireResponseOriginType Where the current answer has came from - AI: generated by Vanta AI - Manual: written in by a user - Original questionnaire: included in the original import - Answer library: the answer was found in a matching question in the knowledge center - Resource: the answer was found in a matching excerpt from a document in the knowledge center
---@field answerSchema? string JSON Schema describing the expected answer format for this question. Prefer `answerPartsSchema` + `answerPartsValues` — those mirror the apps/web GraphQL surface and let clients render against the canonical composite schema.
---@field answerPartsSchema? vanta.manage_vanta.JSONSchema7 Composite JSONSchema7 built from the response's stored answer parts (via `toCompositeSchema`). Mirrors the GraphQL `answerPartsSchema` field. Absent when the response has no stored parts — clients fall back to the legacy `answerSchema` field.
