---@class vanta.manage_vanta.UpdateRiskScenarioRequest
---@field riskScenarioId string
---@field description? string This describes an actual or potential risk to your organization's people, processes, technology, data, and facilities. Document actual issues or likely scenarios based on your specific environment or a potential vulnerability.
---@field detailedDescription? string Optional long-form description providing extended context for the risk scenario. Maximum 10000 characters.
---@field isSensitive? boolean If set to true this risk can only be seen by its owner or users with Admin, RiskSensitiveManage or RiskSensitiveView permissions.
---@field likelihood? number Represents the probability of an incident occurring due to this risk or vulnerability, expressed as a numerical score. Defaults to a range of 1-5, where higher values indicate greater likelihood. The range can be customized in the Risk Management settings.
---@field impact? number Represents the potential severity of harm to your organization’s operations if this risk is exploited, expressed as a numerical score. Defaults to a range of 1-5, where higher values indicate greater impact. The range can be customized in the Risk Management settings.
---@field residualLikelihood? number Represents the adjusted probability of this risk being exploited or affecting operations after implementing risk treatments, such as controls or mitigations. Expressed as a numerical score, defaulting to a range of 1-5. The range can be customized in the Risk Management settings.
---@field residualImpact? number Represents the adjusted severity of harm to your organization’s operations if this risk is exploited after implementing risk treatments, such as controls or mitigations. Expressed as a numerical score, defaulting to a range of 1-5. The range can be customized in the Risk Management settings.
---@field categories? vanta.manage_vanta.UpdateRiskScenarioRequestCategoriesList The list of categories this risk scenario belongs to. Each element in the list will become a new custom category if it doesn't match an existing one. You can reference the current category options in the Risk Management settings and/or enter new values.
---@field ciaCategories? vanta.manage_vanta.UpdateRiskScenarioRequestCiaCategoriesList Enter a list of the following for the type of risk documented: - Confidentiality: Risk to data stores, customer/sensitive information, etc. - Integrity: Risk to accuracy or integrity of system settings and/or data - Availability: Risk to normal service operations and critical system functionality
---@field treatment? vanta.manage_vanta.Treatment|string Indicate how your leadership team wants to address an identified risk. Please note: not all risks need to be addressed immediately (or at all). Your Risk Treatment decision will depend on multiple factors, such as your organization's risk tolerance and the value of the asset that the risk is associated with. The options are: - Mitigate: Identify controls to put in place or tasks to be done that will reduce the risk score. - Transfer: Move risk outside of your organization's set of responsibilities e.g. get cyber liability insurance. - Avoid: Stop doing the activity which is causing the risk to your organization and its assets. - Accept: Decide to live with the risk and take no further actions. - Accept: decide to live with the risk; this may be because it is highly unlikely, has a low financial or operational impact, or the cost and effort to treat the risk far exceeds the value of the asset
---@field owner? string|distilled.Null The person responsible for tracking and mitigating this risk scenario. This should be the email address of a valid Vanta user.
---@field note? string Additional context about the risk scenario and why it has specific impact and likelihood scores.
---@field riskRegister? string Name of the risk register to associate with this scenario.
---@field customFields? vanta.manage_vanta.UpdateRiskScenarioRequestCustomFieldsList The list of custom fields. You can reference custom fields in the Risk Management settings and/or create new one. The format is: - {label: "field-name", value: "string-representation"} for text, date, number and currency fields - {label: "field-name", value: ["option1", "option2"]} for picklist fields If the organization doesn't have custom fields, a non-empty list is rejected and an empty list is ignored.
---@field type? vanta.manage_vanta.RiskScenarioType|string Changing the risk scenario type (`"Risk Scenario"` vs. `"Enterprise Risk"`) is not supported via update. Requests that include this field will be rejected. To change a risk's type, create a new scenario with the desired type and archive the old one.
---@field identificationDate? string The date this risk was identified. Matches the "Identified Date" field in the Vanta UI. Omitting the field leaves the existing value unchanged.

